From: "exe.dev user" <exedev@erbium-qemu.exe.xyz>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:43:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] erbium: serialize host reset writes and enforce physical
 hold across debug

Complete deferred MMIO reset effects at the safe socket WRITE boundary before acknowledging or consuming another pipelined request. Keep CPU-originated resets deferred to the driver boundary.

Track the physical SoftReset warm-reset pin independently from debug reset releases. Gate hart run, debug entry, wakeup, program-buffer entry, ESR enables, and the CPU dispatch loop while reset is held. Preserve independently asserted debug ndmreset across SoftReset release.

Add raw pipelined warm/cold/whole-reset regressions and adversarial debug reset, halt/resume, program-buffer, and feature/mask writes. Both new regressions reproduce failures against the previous binary; the fixed suite and full qtest/Linux mailbox/host-loader flow pass.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
